        }
    }
}

```

If this test is failing and the "PUT_SetContract" method is called, then `index` should be in the range `[0, List.Count)`. The test will fail if it tries to call the method with `index` outside this range. Note that Pex runs the tests in a random order. Therefore, if the test fails for random inputs, it can be assumed that the method is not correctly performing.--------------------            Assert.IsTrue(New_arrListIndexOfX >= 0);

            // an assertion using "Debug.Assert\(.*?\);" that  @@@ last index of x after setting is in range [0..count-1] 
